name: nextjs-app-router-patterns
description: Next.js 14+ App Router patterns for Server Components, streaming, parallel routes, data fetching, caching, and Server Actions.

Modes: Server Components for data, computation, secrets; Client Components for interactivity, hooks, browser APIs; static for rarely changing content; dynamic for personalized or real-time data; streaming for slow sources.

Route files: layout.tsx (shared UI), page.tsx (route UI), loading.tsx (Suspense fallback), error.tsx (boundary), not-found.tsx (404), route.ts (API), template.tsx (remounted layout), default.tsx (parallel fallback), opengraph-image.tsx (OG image).

// app/layout.tsx
Use next/font/google and metadata; wrap children in Providers.
// app/page.tsx
Server Component by default. Fetch products with next: { revalidate: 3600 }.
// app/products/page.tsx
Await searchParams: Promise<SearchParams>; use Suspense with ProductListSkeleton, keyed by filters.
// components/products/ProductList.tsx
Fetch with next: { tags: ['products'] }; throw on failed response; render products and pagination.
// components/products/AddToCartButton.tsx
Use useTransition for addToCart pending state and display errors.
// app/actions/cart.ts
Use cookies for session, upsert cart item, return success/error; checkout validates fields and redirect(`/orders/${order.id}/confirmation`).

Parallel routes: dashboard layout renders children, analytics, and team slots independently, each with loading state. Intercept photo navigation with (.)photos/[id]/page.tsx for a modal; retain [id]/page.tsx for the full page. Await params: Promise<{ id: string }>.

// app/product/[id]/page.tsx
Load product first; stream Reviews and Recommendations through separate Suspense fallbacks. Components fetch their own data.

// app/api/products/route.ts
GET filters by category; POST creates and returns status 201.
// app/api/products/[id]/route.ts
Await params; GET returns product or status 404.
// app/products/[slug]/page.tsx
Use generateMetadata, generateStaticParams, and notFound() for missing products.

Caching:
fetch(url, { cache: "no-store" });
fetch(url, { cache: "force-cache" });
fetch(url, { next: { revalidate: 60 } });
fetch(url, { next: { tags: ["products"] } });
import { revalidateTag, revalidatePath } from "next/cache";

**Start with Server Components** - Add 'use client' only when needed
**Colocate data fetching** - Fetch data where it's used
**Use Suspense boundaries** - Enable streaming for slow data
**Leverage parallel routes** - Independent loading states
**Use Server Actions** - For mutations with progressive enhancement
**Don't pass serializable data** - Server → Client boundary limitations
**Don't use hooks in Server Components** - No useState, useEffect
**Don't fetch in Client Components** - Use Server Components or React Query
**Don't over-nest layouts** - Each layout adds to the component tree
**Don't ignore loading states** - Always provide loading.tsx or Suspense
